# Owner does not want Grok (learned 2026-09-25)

Owner said **2026-08-19** (accounting chat): **“Grok을 사용하고 싶지 않아.”** After Grok broke accounting (IndexedDB date folds, 500s). That was a model-picker preference, not only a coding-style note (`accounting-stable-edits.mdc`).

## Why this chat can still be Grok

A Korean/English sentence in chat **does not** change Cursor Settings. The Agent cannot switch or lock the picker.

Cursor can put Grok on a later turn without the owner clicking it:

| Mechanism | What happens |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Cursor Default** | App open / new chat uses the **recommended** model (Grok 4.6/4.7 class). Staff: this is a product nudge. |
| **Default Model reverts** | “Last Used” can reset to “Cursor Default” after an update (forum, Sep 2026). |
| **Auto** | Auto may **route** to Grok even after leaving Grok in the picker. |
| **Ctrl+N** | New Agent chat via Ctrl+N has jumped to Grok while the **+** button kept Auto. |

This long thread continuing after a compact does **not** mean the owner chose Grok. Do not treat “current model is Grok” as consent.

## Do

- If this session is Grok: say so once, then tell them to switch the **chat model picker** (and Settings below). Keep working only if they stay.
- Pin: **Cursor Settings → Agents → Conversation → Default Model → Last Used**, then pick Claude / Composer / GPT — not Auto if they want Grok fully out.
- Also **Settings → Models**: disable Grok. Disabled models should not be selected.
- New chat: use the Agent **+** button, not Ctrl+N, until that bug is gone.

## Do not

- Assume the owner switched to Grok on purpose.
- Claim a project rule can stop Cursor routing to Grok — only the picker + Last Used + disable Grok can.
- Re-enable Grok “to try the new default.”
